! Glycine conformer I / Gly-Ip, Cs semiexperimental benchmark.
! Geometry: Cartesian Gly-Ip reference structure from the local JPCL agreement
! supporting geometry set, reordered as:
! 1 methylene C, 2 amino N, 3 amino H, 4 carboxyl C, 5 carbonyl O,
! 6 hydroxyl O, 7 hydroxyl H, 8-9 methylene H, 10 amino H.
! Rotational constants are reconstructed from Kasalova et al. Table 3:
! parent constants from the bracketed experimental parent values and isotope
! shifts for 13C(3), 13C(1), C(1)-d2, and 15N. dbvib rows are the Gly-Ip
! zero-point corrections Ae-A0, Be-B0, Ce-C0 from Table 8.
! The four reduced-dimensionality constraints are the Gly-Ip constraints of
! Kasalova et al. Table 5. Unit least-squares weights are used because the
! complete old-isotopologue uncertainty table is not available in this local
! benchmark source bundle.

